WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:13.230
65. The Terracotta Army. Ying Zheng was born in 259 B.C., a time of great chaos and fighting

2
00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:19.270
in Chinese history. Ying was a part of the Qing Dynasty, which united China for the first

3
00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:26.030
time. Ying became the first emperor of China and renamed himself First Emperor Qin Shi

4
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:33.270
Huang. First Emperor had spent his entire life fighting, so perhaps it makes sense that

5
00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:40.510
he went into the afterlife prepared to fight. When he was 13 or 14 years old, the emperor

6
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:47.230
ordered the construction of a massive terracotta army for his tomb, and he specifically stated

7
00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:55.670
that no two soldiers were to look alike. Craftsmen began the great task. Arms, legs,

8
00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:02.150
and torsos were made in molds and assembled later. The soldiers are all life-sized, between

9
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:08.470
5 feet 8 inches and 6 feet 2 inches tall. The faces are of eight different basic types,

10
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:14.950
which were then modified to make each face distinct. Some people believe the faces were

11
00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:21.830
modeled after real Qing warriors. Their clothing and hairstyles reflect their different ranks. The

12
00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:28.870
soldiers are fierce-looking and lifelike. The soldiers were placed in a massive city of the

13
00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:36.070
dead that First Emperor built for himself. Around 700,000 workers built the emperor's great resting

14
00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:42.830
place. The city included a palace, administrative buildings, and anything else the emperor might

15
00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:50.270
need, including his army. Archaeologists have found more than 1,000 warriors so far, but they

16
00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:57.270
estimate that there are 7,000 or 8,000 of them in total. There are also horses, chariots, and weapons.

17
00:01:57.670 --> 00:02:04.310
The army is arranged tactically as though it is ready to spring into battle. A warrior from

18
00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:10.190
beginning to end, First Emperor would not be defeated, not even in death.
